<title>SLOVAKIA: SLOVAK FINMIN 41-WK T-BILL AVE YIELD 11.94 PCT.</title>
<headline>SLOVAK FINMIN 41-WK T-BILL AVE YIELD 11.94 PCT.</headline>
<dateline>BRATISLAVA 1996-12-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Average yield at the Slovak Finance Ministry's auction of 41-week treasury bills hit 11.94 percent, up from 11.25 percent in the last auction of T-bills with a similar maturity, the central bank said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>It added that all 1.095 billion crowns worth of bids at the ministry's three-week T-bill auction were rejected. The ministry does not announce the amount of bills on offer at its auctions.  </p>
<p>					 Dec 4	Nov 27</p>
<p> T-bill maturity		 41-week    40-week</p>
<p> Bids (in billion crowns)	2.570	1.835</p>
<p> Bids accepted		     2.520	1.030</p>
<p> Minimum yield (pct)	    11.4	 10.50</p>
<p> Average yield (pct)	    11.94	11.249</p>
<p> Maximum yield (pct)	    12.50	11.49</p>
<p> Maturity date	     Sept 18, 1997   Sept 4, 1997</p>
<p>-- Bratislava Newsroom, 42-7-563-3687</p>
